# Build artefacts
build/
# Cargo's build directory. Cargo.lock is NOT ignored: DISTRIBUTION.md commits
# to reproducible builds, and with zero dependencies the lock file costs
# nothing and records that fact rather than leaving it to be assumed.
target/
*.o
*.elf
*.uf2
*.bin
*.map

# Dependency symlinks are created by tools/setup_links.sh, never committed —
# a committed symlink dangles on any machine with a different layout, and
# fails later as something that looks like a toolchain problem.
deps/

# Bench logs: truncated per run and regenerated. Captures under
# tests/captures/ ARE committed — they are replay fixtures, not output.
tests/logs/
__pycache__/

# Reference binaries live OUTSIDE this repository entirely (see
# tools/fetch_oracle.sh). Should a local path ever be used, it is never
# committed: running a program creates no derivative work, but vendoring its
# code would place copyleft-licensed files in this repository's history.
oracle/

# The resume / hand-off document is a working note for whoever picks this up
# next, not a published artifact. Deliberately untracked: it names bench paths,
# half-finished threads and the state of open questions, none of which belong
# in a repository that publishes as clean-room. It is also exactly the kind of
# file that would need the check_cleanroom.sh exemption list widened for it.
RESUME.md

# Session instructions, auto-loaded from disk by the assistant. Untracked for
# the same reason RESUME.md is: it points at bench paths and an out-of-tree
# oracle directory, and it is working guidance rather than a published
# artifact. Tracking and loading are independent — this still loads.
CLAUDE.md

# ESP-IDF build output for tests/instrument/. Source and sdkconfig.defaults are
# tracked; everything the toolchain generates is not.
tests/instrument/**/build/
tests/instrument/**/sdkconfig
tests/instrument/**/sdkconfig.old

# Release artifacts. Built on demand by tools/release.sh, never committed --
# a binary in git is a binary nobody rebuilt.
/dist/
